        (id . "R4-F7")
        (resolution . "FIXED by re-measurement with the correct instrument. The sweep now runs racket scripts/run-tests.rkt per file - the runner whose exit code reporting.rkt actually gates on - and reports 376 tests, 376 passed, 0 failed, 0 timeouts, every file exit 0, and 0 files with no test count. The capture carries the runner's own Tests:/Files: lines and each exit code, so a vacuous green is detectable rather than assumed absent, and its header records the full instrument history including that a fourth false alarm came from the capture script's own detector grepping for raco test's summary shape instead of the runner's. This is the same trap as R1-F1 and R4-F1, caught a third time and finally at the level of the instrument itself.")
        (severity . "blocking")
        (summary . "The wrong instrument. The 19-file sweep that substantiates release-preflight.json's 0-failures claim was run with bare raco test, which is wrong twice over: it exits 0 even when a case fails, and for a file whose entry point is module+ main rather than module+ test it executes nothing and still exits 0. Two of the 19 files are shaped that way - test-deterministic-clock.rkt (10 cases) and test-wave-delivery-integrity-register.rkt (10 cases) - so their greens were vacuous: a pass that ran zero tests. The capture recorded zero lines of output for exactly those two files, which is what finally exposed it.")
