    #hasheq(
      (findings . (
        #hasheq(
          (id . "R5-F1")
          (resolution . "FIXED. The stale block is gone: 27 top-level pairs, 27 unique keys, zero duplicates, rebuilt through Racket's own writer so neither duplicates nor malformed structure can survive. implementation-sha now equals the evidence record's, so the gate's cross-record comparison passes. Verified by running the real gate the way CI runs it: eight structural rejections before the fix, two after, and the two remaining are the legitimate pending-review blocks. Four further defects surfaced by running that gate are recorded as R5-F1b through R5-F1e.")
          (severity . "blocking")
          (summary . "The validation record carried eight duplicated top-level keys, and the values the wave gate consumes were a stale trailing block naming content head 86002515 instead of b9a0ac1ad. The reviewer's stated mechanism - that Racket's reader rejects duplicate keys, leaving the record unparseable - is incorrect, and the true mechanism is worse. Racket does not reject duplicate keys in a #hasheq literal: it silently keeps the last. So the record read cleanly, reported 25 unique keys, and passed every structural check, while the gate compared the stale implementation-sha against the evidence record's and would have failed. The reviewer correctly identified the blocking consequence and the stale head; only the mechanism, and therefore the fix, differ.")
        )
        #hasheq(
          (id . "R5-F1b")
          (resolution . "FIXED. implementation-sha is 3a3d3297fe5172c26303a159a67a187e4639a459, matching the evidence record and the head-coherence text in the same datum.")
          (severity . "blocking")
          (summary . "implementation-sha named 86002515f9de49d4abd83d83fd279656ab7c15e7, a superseded content head, while the same record's head-coherence text and the other two records named b9a0ac1ad. The gate requires validation's implementation-sha to equal the evidence record's, so this alone would have been rejected - pointing at a field whose stale value was itself an artifact of the duplicate-key shadowing.")
        )
        #hasheq(
          (id . "R5-F1c")
          (resolution . "FIXED, both with measurements taken at this head rather than quoted. format-compile: raco make and raco fmt canonicality (the same test scripts/pre-commit.rkt performs) over all 29 changed .rkt files between base 50bdf7334 and this head - 29 compiled, 29 canonical, 0 not-canonical, 0 fmt-error. fast: promoted to the top level from suites.fast, with its provenance noted. The nested copy is retained so the record still shows where the number came from.")
          (severity . "blocking")
          (summary . "The record had no top-level format-compile field and no top-level fast field, both required by the gate's validation-required-fields and both then validated for a passed result. The fast measurement existed but only nested under suites, which the gate does not consult - so the record carried a true number in a place no gate would ever read it.")
        )
        #hasheq(
          (id . "R5-F1d")
          (resolution . "FIXED without flattening away the meaning. The first item is genuinely deferred by design and is now classified deferred-noncritical; the other four are noncritical. Each keeps its original descriptive classification in a new label field, so nothing descriptive is lost and the gate sees the vocabulary it requires.")
          (severity . "blocking")
          (summary . "The five remaining-items used descriptive classifications - deferred-by-design, environmental-not-a-regression, follow-up-not-blocking, verdict-bounded, outstanding-coordinator-owned - none of which valid-noncritical-remaining-item? accepts. That predicate admits exactly noncritical and deferred-noncritical. The items were truthful and each carried a nonempty owner and rationale; only the vocabulary was wrong, so the gate rejected the whole list.")
        )
        #hasheq(
          (id . "R5-F1e")
          (resolution . "FIXED; recorded here as the provenance of R5-F1b through R5-F1d, which were found by running the gate rather than by reading the record. The lesson is this wave's recurring one, one level up again: a check that passes is not a check that ran. The record satisfied every read-based inspection available to a reviewer without a shell, and was simultaneously rejected by the project's own gate. A reviewer without exec can confirm a record is well-formed; it cannot confirm a record is accepted.")
          (severity . "blocking")
          (summary . "The round-5 reviewer had no exec tool, so five of the eight gate rejections were invisible to it. Running the gate the way CI does surfaced them: the missing format-compile and fast fields, the implementation-sha mismatch, and the remaining-items vocabulary. Each is a real defect that would have failed CI's evidence gate on the merge candidate.")
        )
        #hasheq(
          (id . "R5-F2")
          (resolution . "FIXED. Round 4's reviewed-sha is 2428611c392f0feec595c3e881beb88536ca52c6, with a note that this is the head when it ran. Worth stating plainly: this was the head-attribution defect class reintroduced while remediating that same class, by rebinding the trio and letting the head field follow the new binding instead of the review that actually happened.")
          (severity . "moderate")
          (summary . "Round 4's reviewed-sha had been rewritten to b9a0ac1ad7771306cda061a3ca4e9a4d3ee29278, a commit created at 01:31:48 local, thirty-nine minutes after the 00:52:24 commit that recorded round 4. The head round 4 reviewed was 2428611c3. Rounds 1 through 3 each keep their true head; round 4 was the only one that did not.")
        )
