      (note . "Round 5 ran to completion and returned CHANGES-REQUESTED. Every finding it raised is enumerated in the findings list below, each reproduced against the tree before being fixed. It reviewed at b9a0ac1ad, the content head current when it ran. The reviewer had no exec tool and worked from the worktree's git metadata and the retained artifacts; everything checkable by reading, it checked, and the substantive test evidence - the 376-test sweep, the playwright failure's honest description, the head-coherence claim, and the R4-F5 trade-off - survived its attack. It judged the R4-F5 deferral legitimate rather than an evasion: the missing metadata is measured, the file's four tests are green, and editing a test file after the chain would have destroyed the no-test-file-changed guarantee the rest of the record depends on. Its one blocking finding was correct in substance and wrong in mechanism, and the correction mattered: the validation record was not unparseable but silently stale, a harder failure to notice and a more dangerous one to ship.")
