      (note . "Round 7 ran to completion and returned CHANGES-REQUESTED with seven findings, all reproduced against the tree and all fixed. Its value is that it caught the REMEDIATION rather than the work: five of its seven findings were stale summary fields in these records, and it showed the round-5 and round-6 fixes for exactly that class were stale by construction - each was written in the same commit that recorded the round it referred to, so each was a round behind the moment it landed. R6-F4, R6-F5 and R6-F6 each reproduced the defect they were filed against, one round later, which is the strongest evidence yet that the defect is the hand-written number and not the number. The fix is therefore to stop restating the count: the evidence status and the validation notes now name this record as the authority and say nothing that can fall behind, and this verdict's counts are derived from the findings it contains. The remaining two findings were real measurement errors - the manifest totals were not updated when the captures grew the manifest, and the chain and head-coherence enumerations were not updated when the same captures were added - and both are now measured against the ranges the merge candidate actually spans. R7-F7 caught the record claiming the new captures were measured at the binding head when they name an earlier one, which is this campaign's own rule, restated after being broken.")
