      (note . "Round 8 ran to completion and returned CHANGES-REQUESTED. All of its substantive findings were one class, and the class is procedural rather than textual: the records bound head 4891dd2a while four present-tense sentences still described 3a3d3297f as the content head. That is not four separate oversights - it is a gap in the rebind procedure, which updated the binding fields and not the prose naming the same head, so every rebind this wave created a fresh class of self-contradiction. The sharpest instance was the evidence record's merge authorization, which instructed that an APPROVED review be bound at a head the gate itself rejects; an operator following it literally would have produced a binding that could not pass. Rounds 6, 7 and 8 each found defects introduced by the previous round's remediation. That is a convergence failure and is recorded as one. What converges is the content: every measurement round 8 could re-derive checked out - the capture totals, the manifest counts, the suite numbers, the reflog timestamps, the gate's structure, and both enumerations, which held at thirteen and fourteen once measured against the right endpoint. The rebind procedure is now hardened to report any superseded head still named as a live claim, so the next rebind fails loudly rather than silently.")
