      (note . "Round 9 ran to completion with a shell available and was the first round whose checks were executed rather than simulated. That difference is the substantive result of this round: the digest, record-commit, verify, the wave gate, all three manifests, provenance and lint were run, and every numeric claim in the three records was independently re-derived. All five checks executed green, and the gate reported exactly the two expected rejections with no third hiding behind them - confirmed by reading the gate source, which appends to reasons without short-circuiting. Every measurement held: both path enumerations matched the actual path SETS and not merely the counts, the suite numbers matched raw/verify-chain.txt, the capture file lists matched git, and the affected sweep still read 376/376 with every runner exit 0. Round 9 also swept all fourteen superseded heads across the three records and confirmed every occurrence is either a per-round reviewed-sha by design, a historical finding, or a capture attribution naming the tree it ran on - no live field names a superseded head. Its four findings are prose-integrity, in the review record's own fields and in one test comment, and none touches binding, digest, checksum, provenance or measurement. The first is damage this record's own remediation did three commits earlier, which is the convergence pattern stated again: a text-position edit to a record that repeats the same value corrupted a field, the doubling was caught, and the mangled note was not. Round 10 is pending.")
