        #hasheq(
          (id . "W7-R10-F2")
          (resolution . "FIXED at the source. The per-round findings arrays are the data and the aggregate is derived prose, so the nine-round total was corrected from 56 to 55 rather than a finding being invented to reach 56, and this round's two findings bring the derived total to 57. The record now also says where the off-by-one came from: the round-8 aggregate was hand-maintained, and the correction is made by summing the arrays, which is the only derivation that cannot drift. Asserted on the parsed record, not on the text.")
          (severity . "moderate")
          (summary . "The verdict aggregate was wrong, and had been wrong since round 8. It read all 56 findings; the nine per-round findings arrays sum to 55. Rounds 1 through 8 sum to 51, not the 52 the record had been carrying, so the error was inherited rather than introduced by round 9 - the 56 came from adding four to a total that was already one high.")
